        walkthrough = 'Head to Heavens Tower in Windurst Walls HP #1.\n1. Click the Door: Vestal Chamber at the top of the Tower to start the Mission and to receive [Key Item] New Fei\'Yin seal.\n   - If you are low level, you might want to use Trusts or form a party of lvl 50+ players.\n2. Go to Fei\'Yin (located in the northeast corner of Beaucedine Glacier) for a cutscene with Zeid. You will have to reach the Qu\'Bia Arena and clear the BCNM "The Rank 5 Mission".\n   - The majority of enemies in Fei\'Yin detect by  sound, however there are several that detect  spellcasting.\n   - Quick Travel options:\n     - Home Point #1 to Fei\'Yin is the fastest way, it puts you right at the zone to Qu\'Bia Arena.\n     - Unity Warp (Level 128) will place you at the entrance of Fei\'Yin.\n     - Unity Warp (Level 125) will place you in the central area of Beaucedine Glacier.\n   - From the entrance of Fei\'Yin:\n     - Go east to (K-8). There are 2 Dolls in front of a door named Cermet Portal, open it and you\'ll be able to enter Qu\'Bia Arena.\nYou will be able to prepare outside of the BC, however all buffs will wear upon entering. Plan accordingly and click the Burning Circle when ready.\n3. You only need to kill the Archlich to win.\n4. You will be facing Archlich Taber\'quoan. The Archlich will spawn with 2 Ancient Sorcerers. Ancient Warriors will also spawn in the hallway and run into the arena to help the Archlich during the fight.\n   - The Archlich is a BLM, and will cast spells like Sleepga II and Freeze, he may also use Manafont.\n   - The lesser skeletons have very little HP and can be easily taken out by an AoE spell.\n   - Focus attacks on the Archlich, a Paladin with Invincible is useful for managing the many extra mobs. A Monk using Hundred Fists also shines in this fight, due to the skeleton blunt penalty.\n5. When you win, you\'ll be given another cutscene and receive [Key Item] Burnt seal.\nYou can head back to the Heavens Tower.\n6. Check the Door: Vestal Chamber at the top to complete the Mission.',
        notes = nil,
    },
    ['The Heart of the Matter'] = {
        id = 1,
        start_npc = 'Any Windurst Gate Guard',
        start_zone = 'Windurst Waters',
        start_pos = 'F-5',
        description = 'Assist the Manustery in the creation of Cardians. You must go to the southeastern magic tower of the Horutoto Ruins in East Sarutabaruta, and energize the Mana Orbs that serve as the hearts of the Cardians. Inquire at the Manustery first for details.',
        reward = 'Rank Points',
        fame = nil,
        fame_level = nil,
        title = nil,
        repeatable = 'No',
        previous = {'The Horutoto Ruins Experiment'},
        next = {'The Price of Peace'},
        requirements = nil,
        walkthrough = '1. Accept the Mission from any Gate Guard.\n   - Mokyokyo - Windurst Waters (F-5)\n   - Janshura-Rashura - Port Windurst (B-5)\n   - Rakoh Buuma - Windurst Woods (K-10)\n   - Zokima-Rokima - Windurst Walls (H-7)\n2. Then make your way to the Manustery in Windurst Woods, Speak to Apururu who is at (H-9).\n   - You may need to talk to her twice if you have a [Key Item] Windurst Trust permit as she will mention talking to her brother, Ajido-Marujido.\n3. You will receive the following Mana Orbs Key Items:\n   - [Key Item] First dark Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Second dark Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Third dark Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Fourth dark Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Fifth dark Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Sixth dark Mana Orb\n4. You are now instructed to go to the Outer Horutoto Ruins.\n5. Head to (J-11) in East Sarutabaruta and speak to Pore-Ohre at the entrance to Marguerite Tower, they will give you the [Key Item] Southeastern star charm.\n   - Make sure you get this, or you will be unable to energize the orbs later on.\n6. Check the six pedestals to place a Mana Orb.\n   - Examine the Cracked Walls along the north and south sides to find hidden rooms, which contain 2 more pedestals for your Mana Orbs.\n7. After all orbs have been set, pass through the Cracked Wall on the east side and then examine the Gate: Magical Gizmo behind it for a cutscene.\n8. After the cutscene, check each pedestal again to retrieve the 6 Glowing Mana Orb Key Items:\n   - [Key Item] First glowing Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Second glowing Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Third glowing Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Fourth glowing Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Fifth glowing Mana Orb\n   - [Key Item] Sixth glowing Mana Orb\n9. When you\'ve collected all 6, head back out of the tower. When you zone, you\'ll receive another cutscene.\n   - (Optional): You can speak to Quh Berhuja nearby for some dialogue.\n   - Alternatively, you can use any means of leaving the zone that will not lead you to East Sarutabaruta. Doing this will allow you to skip the cutscene and go straight back to Apururu will which lead to a slightly different cutscene upon finishing the Mission.\n10. Head back to the Manustery and speak to Apururu to complete the Mission.',
        notes = nil,
    },
    ['The Horutoto Ruins Experiment'] = {
        id = 0,
        start_npc = 'Any Windurst Gate Guard',
        start_zone = 'Windurst Waters',
        start_pos = 'F-5',
        description = 'The minister of the Orastery in conducting an experiment in the eastern magic tower of the Horutoto Ruins, located in East Sarutabaruta. Inquire at the Orastery first, then go assist him.',
        reward = 'Rank Points',
        fame = nil,
        fame_level = nil,
        title = 'Title based on :Category:Gate Guard',
        repeatable = 'No',
        previous = nil,
        next = {'The Heart of the Matter'},
        requirements = nil,
        walkthrough = '1. Speak to any Windurstian Gate Guard, and accept the Mission.\n   - Mokyokyo - Windurst Waters (F-5)\n   - Janshura-Rashura - Port Windurst (B-5)\n   - Rakoh Buuma - Windurst Woods (K-10)\n   - Zokima-Rokima - Windurst Walls (H-7)\n2. Head for the Orastery in Port Windurst. Speak to Hakkuru-Rinkuru at (E-7) for a cutscene.\n3. Make your way to (J-7) in East Sarutabaruta. You\'re looking for a large stone tower.\n   - The Inner Horutoto Ruins Survival Guide places you at the right tower if you have it unlocked already.\n4. (Optional): Speak to Sama Gohjima near the entrance for some dialogue.\n5. Head down the stairs to the Inner Horutoto Ruins.\n6. Inside, you\'ll be in the Lily Tower on Map 1. Go down the stairs in to the main room.\n7. Run to the other side, and look for the Cracked Wall, around (H-9). Pass through it and go left.\n8. Check the Gate: Magical Gizmo at (I-9) for a cutscene with the Minister.\n9. Now, head back out and check the six different Ancient Magical Gizmos until you are given the [Key Item] Cracked Mana Orb. It will be at a random Gizmo.\n10. Head back to Hakkuru-Rinkuru and speak with him to finish the Mission.',
        notes = nil,
    },
    ['The Jester Who\'d Be King'] = {
        id = 21,
        start_npc = 'Any Windurst Gate Guard',
        start_zone = 'Windurst Woods',
        start_pos = nil,
        description = 'The time for the Dark Dungeon jailbreak is at hand! At the request of the Manustery, you are to collect the ministry rings from all five ministers.',
        reward = 'Rank 9\n80,000 Gil',
        fame = nil,
        fame_level = nil,
        title = 'None',
        repeatable = 'No',
        previous = {'Vain'},
        next = {'Doll of the Dead'},
        requirements = nil,
        walkthrough = 'Trade enough Crystals to the Conquest NPC to raise the Rank bar and unlock the Mission, then accept it from the Gate Guard.\n1. Talk to Apururu in Windurst Woods HP #1 inside the northern Manustery building for a cutscene. You will obtain the [Key Item] Manustery ring.\n2. Talk to the following NPCs, in any order, to receive the [Key Item] Rhinostery ring, [Key Item] Aurastery ring, and [Key Item] Optistery ring:\n   - Rukususu in Fei\'Yin at (F-6) on Map #2. Click the Cermet Door of the north-western small room for a cutscene with her.\n     - Home Point #2 to Fei\'Yin is the fastest way.\n   - Sedal-Godjal in Davoi (J-8). He can only be reached by going through Monastic Cavern. Enter Monastic Cavern from entrance 2 at (H-11) in Davoi. Once you\'re in, hug the right wall and exit at (H/I-8). Once you\'re back in Davoi, you can reach Sedal-Godjal by going east.\n     - Proto-Waypoint to Davoi is the fastest way. Drop into the water, follow the water south-east to (J-10) to get back on land, then hug left until you reach entrance 2.\n     - Survival Guide to Davoi is almost as fast.\n   - Tosuka-Porika in Windurst Waters North HP #1, inside the eastern Optistery building.\n3. Return to Apururu for dialogue regarding the final ring.\n----\n4. Talk to Kupipi in Heavens Tower for a cutscene.\n5. Go to the tower in West Sarutabaruta (F-4) and enter Outer Horutoto Ruins.\n   - Outer Horutoto Ruins Voidwatch warp or West Sarutabaruta\'s Geomagnetic Fount puts you right in front of this tower.\n   - Warping to the outpost/Survival Guide for West Sarutabaruta or warping to Giddeus and using Escape are the next best options.\n6. Go through the Cracked Wall at (I-6).\n7. Find the Cracked Wall at (G-8) on the second map. Touch it and pop Queen of Coins (RDM) and Queen of Swords (PLD).\n8. Click the Cracked Wall again (multiple times if needed) after defeating them for a cutscene and to obtain the [Key Item] Orastery ring.\n9. Return to Apururu for a cutscene.\n10. Talk to Shantotto in Windurst Walls at (K-7) for a cutscene and to obtain the [Key Item] Glove of perpetual twilight.\n   - You may need to speak to Shantotto multiple times for the correct cutscene.\n11. Return to Apururu for a cutscene.\n12. Go to Inner Horutoto Ruins and examine the Gate of Darkness at (I-7, south-eastern door) on Map 4 for a cutscene.\n   - Fastest way is using the Toraimarai Canal Survival Guide and then back tracking to Horutoto ruins.\n   - Alternatively, travel though Toraimarai Canal using the Priming Gate in Windurst Walls (H-3).\n   - You need to pass through the Three Mage Gate if you do not enter via the Toraimarai Canal.\n13. Return to Apururu for a cutscene that completes the Mission.\n   - (Optional) Return to Shantotto for dialogue regarding the [Key Item] Glove of perpetual twilight.\n     - Ohohohoho! It looks like my glove of perpetual twilight had the desired effect! Ajido-Marujido\'s failure tor egain consciousness is the only slight complication I was able to detect... But you don\'t need to go and start worrying. Why, it would take mor than that to finish of fa mage that had survived my tutelage and training! ...Now, about the glove of perpetual twilight. Due to a slight miscalculation on my part, the rings have become fused to the glove, I see. But don\'t worry. With a few twists, I\'ll soon have them free. I\'ll just hold on to the ministry rings for a little while longer. Ohohoho!\n   - (Optional) Return to Tosuka-Porika to report about the Book of the Gods as promised.\n     - Where have you been? Did Ajido-Marujido get the book open!? ...Hrmm, he\'s fallen into a coma, has he...? He must\'ve been drawn into the "World of the Book." If he manages to return to consciousness, he will have all the knowledge contained within the Book of the Gods. ...If he makes it back, that is.',
        notes = nil,
    },
    ['The Price of Peace'] = {
        id = 2,
        start_npc = 'Any Windurst Gate Guard',
        start_zone = 'Windurst Waters',
        start_pos = 'F-5',
        description = 'Recieve two bags of food offerings from the Rhinostery, and deliver one bag to each of the Yagudo who stand by the altars of offerings in Giddeus. Don\'t forget to report back to the Rhinostery after completing the mission.',
        reward = 'Rank 2\n1,000 Gil',
        fame = nil,
        fame_level = nil,
        title = nil,
        repeatable = 'No',
        previous = {'The Heart of the Matter'},
        next = {'Lost for Words'},
        requirements = nil,
        walkthrough = '1. Accept the Mission from any Gate Guard.\n   - Mokyokyo - Windurst Waters (F-5)\n   - Janshura-Rashura - Port Windurst (B-5)\n   - Rakoh Buuma - Windurst Woods (K-10)\n   - Zokima-Rokima - Windurst Walls (H-7)\n2. Then make your way to the roof of the Rhinostery in Windurst Waters (J-8) (near Home Point #3), it is located in the southern half of the zone.\n   - Speak with Leepe-Hoppe at (J-9) on the roof of the Rhinostery. He will give you the [Key Item] Food offering and [Key Item] Drink offering.\n3. Head out for Giddeus, which is located at (F-8) in West Sarutabaruta.\n   - If you previously unlocked it, you can teleport directly to (G-12) with Home Point #1 and make your way north from there.\n4. Make your way to (H-7) and speak to a Yagudo NPC named Laa Mozi to hand over the [Key Item] Food offering.\n   - You can reach this NPC by taking all left turns from the Sarutabaruta entrance.\n5. Next, head to (G-7) and speak to a Yagudo NPC called Ghoo Pakya to hand over the [Key Item] Drink offering.\n   - Return to the Sarutabaruta entrance and take all right turns to reach this NPC.\n6. Head back to the Rhinostery. As you climb the stairs to the roof, you\'ll receive another cutscene.\n7. Return to the Gate Guard to complete the Mission.',
